  {# 2. In 30 seconds, with the release date (QCM of 2026-10-19: merges « Final version ») #}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="conteneur">
      <h2>In 30 seconds</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>AZERTY Global 2026</strong> has been available as a final version since <strong>June&nbsp;15, 2026</strong>:
          a <strong>free and open-source</strong> keyboard layout for Windows, macOS and Linux
          that fixes the historical flaws of the traditional Windows AZERTY with no new hardware. You can finally type
          <strong><a class="lien-caractere" href="/e-aigu-majuscule" hreflang="fr" aria-label="Capital É (in French)">É</a>, <a class="lien-caractere" href="/e-grave-majuscule" hreflang="fr" aria-label="Capital È (in French)">È</a>, <a class="lien-caractere" href="/a-grave-majuscule" hreflang="fr" aria-label="Capital À (in French)">À</a>, <a class="lien-caractere" href="/c-cedille-majuscule" hreflang="fr" aria-label="Capital Ç (in French)">Ç</a></strong> directly with Caps Lock, use
          <strong><a href="/guillemets" hreflang="fr">French quotation marks « »<span class="visuellement-cache"> (in French)</span></a></strong>, and reach
          <strong><a href="/dev" hreflang="fr">programming symbols<span class="visuellement-cache"> (in French)</span></a>, including <a class="lien-caractere" href="/accolades" hreflang="fr" aria-label="Curly braces { } (in French)">{&nbsp;}</a> and <a class="lien-caractere" href="/crochets" hreflang="fr" aria-label="Square brackets [ ] (in French)">[&nbsp;]</a></strong>
          easily. All without upsetting your habits: <strong>only five changes</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# 4. The five changes #}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="conteneur">
      <h2>The five changes</h2>
      <p class="presse-chapo">
        The letters A to Z stay in place: AZERTY Global mainly fixes the access the French keyboard was missing.
      </p>

      <div class="presse-grille presse-grille--changements">
        <div class="presse-carte">
          <h3>Smart Caps Lock</h3>
          <p>Accented capitals in one press: É, È, Ç, À without any shortcut.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="presse-carte">
          <h3>Direct period</h3>
          <p>The period and the semicolon are swapped, in favor of the more frequently used sign.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="presse-carte">
          <h3>Accessible at sign and hash</h3>
          <p>On the top-left key: @ for email addresses, # with Shift.</p>
          <p class="presse-carte__lien"><a href="/arobase" hreflang="fr">All about the at sign<span class="visuellement-cache"> (in French)</span></a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="presse-carte">
          <h3>Accessible developer symbols</h3>
          <p>Access to <a class="lien-caractere" href="/accolades" hreflang="fr" aria-label="Curly braces { } (in French)">{&nbsp;}</a> <span class="insecable">\ |</span> <a class="lien-caractere" href="/crochets" hreflang="fr" aria-label="Square brackets [ ] (in French)">[&nbsp;]</a> with AltGr on D F G H J K, from the home row.</p>
          <p class="presse-carte__lien"><a href="/dev" hreflang="fr">The developers page<span class="visuellement-cache"> (in French)</span></a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="presse-carte">
          <h3>Accents on the ù key</h3>
          <p>Acute ´ and grave ` accents together, to type more languages easily.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

